[00:33.11]Conversation One
[00:34.94]M: Welcome, Eva, for coming to our show tonight. 
[00:38.20]What are you busy with recently?
[00:40.15]W: After eleven and a half months out of the competition scene, it was so much fun to get back on ice, taking two wins this past week. 
[00:48.46]Being away from ice just made me realize how much I miss it, how much I love it and I'm so lucky to get to do what I do for a living.
[00:56.63]M: Some say balance is one of the keys to a great life. 
[00:59.99]You're an excellent student attending a world-famous university, a professional athlete and model. 
[01:06.26]What's the secret?
[01:07.49]W: I'm really just very passionate about what I do. 
[01:10.52]I'm so lucky that I get to skate, go to school, and do fashion. 
[01:14.88]They are different life paths. 
[01:16.38]But at the same time, they all really relate to one another. 
[01:19.84]For example, in school, I'm learning psychology; I really apply the psychological knowledge to my skating. 
[01:26.65]But then in skating, I'm very creative and expressive, and I really bring that into the fashion industry. 
[01:32.92]And then for fashion, I feel like I'm learning about confidence, and I also apply it in school.
[01:38.99]So it all goes like in a circle. 
[01:41.19]I guess that's the secret.
[01:42.92]M: Now, excellence can't be achieved without some sacrifice. 
[01:46.37]What are some of the things you've sacrificed to make your dream a reality? 
[01:50.67]W: I guess the hardest part is just not being in the same time zone. 
[01:54.34]I travel constantly, and when I'm away, I really miss my parents, my friends and my cats.
[02:00.76]M: I understand. How do you overcome such feelings, then?
[02:04.63]W: Those feelings are overwhelming when I'm away. 
[02:07.10]So when I'm back, I really just make that much more effort to be present and to be caught up with them.
[02:12.95]M: Well, I'm glad you managed to keep the different aspects of your life in balance. 
[02:17.11]Thanks for joining us.
