[03:33.08]Conversation Two
[03:35.71]M: Now joining me is the chief scientist at the Nature Conservancy, Katherine Hayhoe. 
[03:41.33]Katherine, thanks so much for joining us. 
[03:44.17]You say you were shocked by the climate extremes we saw last year.
[03:48.13]W: Yeah. Shocked, but not surprised, because this is exactly what we scientists have been predicting for years and even decades. 
[03:55.93]But seeing it in real life with your own eyes is different from seeing it in a row of tiny numbers on your computer.
[04:02.40]M: True. Then, what are you expecting to see this year?
[04:05.60]W: Well, we expect decade by decade, as the world warms, we are going to see more frequent and more dangerous extremes. 
[04:12.70]But every year is like rolling the dice. 
[04:14.98]Some years you see a little bit less; some years you see a little bit more.
[04:18.88]M: What can we do to change this?
[04:20.73]W: Well, it's easy to feel helpless. 
[04:22.74]You might say, ¡°Well, I recycle, and I change my bulbs. 
[04:25.88]What else am I supposed to do?¡± 
[04:27.81]But the way that each of us can have the biggest impact on our future is using something we all have¡ªour voice. 
[04:34.81]We call for a change. We just can't do it alone. 
[04:37.95]We have to do it together.
[04:39.70]M: A lot of the media coverage around climate change can be really discouraging. 
[04:43.82]Do you see cause for hope though?
[04:45.80]W: Well, when you ask young people how they feel about climate change, the words you get are ¡°sad¡± ¡°angry¡± ¡°frustrated¡± and ¡°depressed¡±. 
[04:53.41]If you actually understand what's happening, you should be worried. 
[04:57.03]But what I do know is that our future is not yet written. 
[05:00.50]Our future is literally in our hands. 
[05:03.08]We truly can shape our future. 
[05:05.28]And that, to me, is the definition of hope.
[05:07.95]M: Thank you so much for being with us. 
[05:09.87]Really appreciate your perspective.
[05:12.48]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.
[05:16.60]5.Why is the woman shocked but not surprised by the climate extremes last year?
