[13:07.49]Recording One
[13:09.49]¡°Depression affects somewhere between 10% and 25% of people. 
[13:14.26]It hurts well-being more than debt, divorce, or diabetes,¡± said Dr. Michael Noetel, senior lecturer in the School of Psychology at the University of Queensland in Australia.
[13:25.58]When a wave of depression hits, exercise may sound like the last thing you want to do. 
[13:31.11]But a new study says it could be crucial to feeling better. 
[13:35.17]Many types of exercise¡ªincluding walking, jogging, yoga, tai chi, aerobic exercises and strength training¡ªshowed benefits as strong as therapy when it came to treating depression, according to the study published Wednesday.
[13:49.92]Researchers analyzed data from 218 studies on exercise and depression, with more than 14,000 people included. 
[13:58.12]While there was risk for bias in the studies, the whole-body benefits of exercise, paired with data to suggest that it helps with depression, make for a strong treatment option. 
[14:08.95]The results align with what many other studies have said about the benefits of exercise. 
[14:14.02]A 2018 study of more than 1.2 million Americans showed those who exercised reported better well-being and mental health.
[14:22.63]Both studies should give people confidence that exercise is a good approach to treating depression along with other options, including therapy and medication. 
[14:31.75]¡°None of these treatments are silver bullets. 
[14:33.97]But, given how frustrating it is to have depression, almost all patients should be offered both exercise and therapy,¡± Noetel said.
[14:42.47]The study found that more exercise and a higher intensity of workout were better, but you don't need to start out training like a professional athlete. 
[14:51.03]The intensity of the exercise made the biggest difference, but even walking had an impact. 
[14:56.64]Any exercise was better than none, but Noetel recommended adding some challenges.
[15:02.23]Many people struggle with finding the motivation to exercise, and adding depression on top of that can make it even harder to get started. 
[15:10.52]You can find those by joining a fitness group, getting a trainer or asking a loved one to go for a walk with you. 
[15:17.18]And whether your thing is weight training or walking, you need to make the activity enjoyable to keep it up. 
[15:23.34]¡°Be kind to your future self by making exercise as easy and attractive as possible, like getting yourself an audiobook or a trial at a yoga studio,¡± Noetel said. 
[15:34.15]The more you enjoy your workout, the more confident you will be to overcome exercise obstacles.
