[16:36.44]Recording Two
[16:38.78]Every year, two thirds of us make New Year's resolutions whether it's starting a diet, quitting smoking or heading to the gym, but when it comes to health and well-being in the coming year, getting your finances in order tops the list. 
[16:51.88]But how? Here are some tips.
[16:54.09]First, draw up a budget plan. 
[16:56.46]With the dawn of a new year, we all start out with good intentions to stick to our goals. 
[17:01.27]But without a long-term strategy in place, they can easily fall by the wayside. 
[17:05.70]You can always ask yourself these two questions, ¡°Do I Need It? Could I Do It More Cheaply?¡± 
[17:11.13]And get your bank statements, household bills and receipts and work out where you can save money. 
[17:16.61]I saved ¡ê600 last year on my car and house insurance simply by shopping around. 
[17:21.88]Customer loyalty seldom pays. 
[17:24.29]Cutting out your ¡ê2.5 weekday coffee could reduce your annual outgoing by ¡ê600.
[17:30.05]Then, look back at last year's spending and see where you made financial mistakes and where you succeeded. 
[17:36.14]Then look at what you hope to achieve financially during the new year. 
[17:39.95]Maybe it's paying off a credit card or finding a way to make some extra cash to put towards a deposit for a mortgage. 
[17:46.12]Always try and pay your bills as soon as they come in to avoid late fees, which, with interest payment, only add to your debt. 
[17:53.60]If you are an impulse shopper, try and put yourself on pause.
[17:57.18]The next to consider is your pension. 
[17:59.69]You are never too young to start a pension. 
[18:01.82]Yes, it might seem like it's years into the future but you will need to put money aside whether through a work pension scheme or a private one. 
[18:09.32]The earlier you start, the lower the payments are likely to be. 
[18:12.69]It might not seem like a priority but a little saved now can make all the difference when it comes to retirement. 
[18:18.58]Putting ¡ê30 extra away a month from the age of 27 could see someone accumulate an extra ¡ê100,000 by the time they reach the current state pension age.
[18:28.52]And finally, what better way to be a great financial role model and keep your resolutions on track than to start saving for your children's future? 
[18:36.46]Small amounts will snowball and give them a nest egg that could help them keep their financial resolutions when they grow up.
[18:42.50]I really hope these tips can help you financially secure in the years to come. 
[18:46.39]Oh, one more thing, don't forget to take advantage of free money when you see it.
